{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr2MpEqSnMw7iPMdFAHo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't confirm this from the snippets. None of them contain the user update path, so these locations are inferred from the symptom and from how this NestJS boilerplate is usually structured. The line ranges are estimates.\n\nEditing only `firstName` makes the stored `photo` come back empty. That points to the update merging a partial DTO into the existing user and then overwriting `photo` with `undefined` or `null`.\n\nThe `firstName` DTO and entity snippets look normal.\n\nThe `UsersController.update` and `create` snippets only pass the DTO to `UsersService`, so they don't cause this.\n\n**Fix:** In `UsersService.update`, only touch `photo` when the DTO actually includes it. Resolve the file only when `updateUserDto.photo` is defined, and don't write `photo: undefined` or `photo: null` for a partial update. Strip undefined keys from the payload before merging. In the persistence mapper, build the `photo` relation or field only when the domain object has a photo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33551c88-03b7-4474-b2c3-b9bbf07daad1","uuid":"26e4a712-d2b1-489e-97c4-0eb2acc6f3af","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:36:57.548Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr2Mp2RxbBPWD6Kgj3Zw"}
